{
  "requirement": "The Habeas Codicem book MUST configure mdBook's Git repository link for `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem` and its page edit links for the `main` branch.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.layout.repository_links` has two obligations. `book.toml` must set mdBook's Git repository link to `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem`. It must also set the page edit links to the `main` branch.\n\nThe test `tests/repository.rs#fn[book_links_to_the_repository_and_main_branch_edit_pages]` has a `{test}` reference to the requirement. It parses `book.toml` through the helper `repository_toml`, which reads the file and parses it as TOML. It then reads `output.habeas.html`, the table where the book sets its HTML options. That table is `table[output.habeas.html]` in `book.toml`, and the `git-repository-url` and `edit-url-template` keys sit under it. The test makes two assertions:\n\n- `git-repository-url` equals `https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem`.\n- `edit-url-template` equals `https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem/edit/main/{path}`.\n\nTogether these cover the repository link and the `main` edit branch. A wrong repository, a wrong branch, or a missing key would fail an assertion. The requirement names no other inputs or failure cases, so I found no gaps.",
